**transportation-priorities → BLANK `direction-only`**

The only source is the chaptered text of SB 960 (2023-2024), authored by Wiener (`own-act`, `record`/`author`, in-term, dated 2024-09-27). It's on-question — it directs where state transportation investment goes across modes — but its operative sections only add complete streets and transit priority requirements *into* the state highway operation and protection program (the rehabilitation program). Nothing in the operative text addresses new road capacity or the balance between modes, so it can't separate rung 1 ("over new road capacity") from rung 2 ("invest equally") or rung 3 ("maintain roads while selectively adding…"). The strong mode-shift language sits in SECTION 1 findings, which are recitals and don't govern (V4.1), and silence about road capacity is not a clause (V4.2).

`needs_source` asks for Wiener's own words on investment priority relative to road capacity, or an instrument whose operative section conditions or redirects road-capacity funding.
